hor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On macOS the entitlement check is definitive. It reads this process’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"own code-signing entitlements, and requires ","type":"text"},{"code":"CloudKit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"com.apple.developer.icloud-services","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" list that is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"non-empty and, when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"containerID"},{"type":"text","text":" is given, names it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS, tvOS, watchOS, and visionOS offer no public API for a process to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read its own entitlements, so there the build is trusted unless you pass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"isEntitled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". That trust is narrower than it sounds: those platforms"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuse to launch a binary claiming entitlements its profile doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grant, so a running build lacks CloudKit only if its entitlements file"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never asked for it — a fact fixed at build time, which surfaces on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".iCloud"},{"type":"text","text":" probe in development. A build that is entitled but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pointed at the wrong container is still caught, from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CKError.badContainer"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".missingEntitlement"},{"type":"text","text":" the accoun